   alt (rho_total/cH0)    0.5     A    0.0384 +/-0.0191    0.0633 +/-0.0180   -0.0250 +/-0.0150     1.7s
   alt (rho_total/cH0)    0.5     B    0.0375 +/-0.0164    0.0583 +/-0.0192   -0.0208 +/-0.0246     0.8s
   alt (rho_total/cH0)    0.7     A   -0.0497 +/-0.0184    0.0012 +/-0.0160   -0.0509 +/-0.0149     3.4s
   alt (rho_total/cH0)    0.7     B   -0.0149 +/-0.0144   -0.0145 +/-0.0201   -0.0004 +/-0.0241     0.0s

   NOTE (trap 6): Chae's residuals are measured against the SIMPLE IF with a0 fitted per part;
   the absolute levels here are against the framework curve at FIXED a0, so the inner/outer
   DIFFERENCE is the comparable number, not the levels.
   Isolation of the pooled-vs-per-galaxy sign difference (canonical, Ud=0.5, split A):
     pooled, all 152 galaxies (incl. all-inner):     diff = -0.0393 +/- 0.0150
     pooled, both-zone subset (114 galaxies):          diff = -0.0425 +/- 0.0149
     per-galaxy equal-weight mean of the SAME statistic:  D_perp = +0.0006 +/- 0.0091
     per-galaxy equal-weight (delta, main statistic):     Dbar   = +0.0024 +/- 0.0105
     inverse-variance-weighted mean of D_g:               D_ivw  = -0.0208 +/- 0.0106
     Dbar split by L36 (median 9.5e9 Lsun): high-L = -0.0047 +/- 0.0122 (N=57), low-L = +0.0095 +/- 0.0173 (N=57)
     => the MG-direction signal is carried entirely by the PRECISION WEIGHTING, not by the
        all-inner galaxies (both-zone pooled diff unchanged) and only mildly by luminosity
        (high-L and low-L means are each consistent with zero). Equal-galaxy weighting of the
        identical residuals gives ~0 (MI-like); precision weighting concentrates the statistic
        in the small-error points of a minority of galaxies and lands near Chae's value and the
        QUMOND prediction. Whether that is physics (MG radius mixing is largest exactly where
        errors are smallest) or error-model artifact (galaxy-coherent inclination/beam/Upsilon
        systematics are NOT in the SPARC per-point errors, so precision weights over-trust
        exactly the points where traps 1-3 live) is NOT decidable from SPARC alone.
   Pooled variant with S/N >= 10 (drops the low-quality inner points Chae kept):
     canonical (cH_Lambda/Z): inner +0.0518, outer +0.0907, diff = -0.0389 +/- 0.0151 (2.6s)
     alt (rho_total/cH0)   : inner +0.0389, outer +0.0634, diff = -0.0245 +/- 0.0154 (1.6s)
